WEBVTT

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.700
Lucky you! This is the last of 'em.

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:11.580
"Truth Discernment"
"Real"       "Fake"

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:11.750
"Truth Discernment"     "Identification"
"Real"       "Fake"

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:12.700
"Truth Discernment"     "Identification"
"Real"

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.200
Thank you kindly!

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.330
The last three, huh? That <i>is</i> lucky.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.330
Hey! Grab her!

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.160
Don't touch me!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.700
Let me go!

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.370
You behave!

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.540
This brat'll fetch us a pile of lir.

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.080
Kidnapping a loli?
Are you trying to start something?

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:36.830
Who the hell are <i>you</i> ?

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.540
Just a passing Journalist.

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.250
And just who do ya think you're talkin' to?

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.870
Hup.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.450
A Journalist who knows martial arts?!

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.120
Wow! You're so strong!

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.080
Are you hurt, young miss?

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:06.330
I'm no "young miss"! I am--

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:07.950
<i>There</i> you are!

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:10.370
She's over here--with a suspicious woman!

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.750
"Suspicious"?

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:15.040
Oh, no! We've got to run, and fast!

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:17.580
Hey! Why drag <i>me</i> into this?

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:18.790
Halt!

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.790
Getting captured would be bad news.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:39.200
It's so sweet and fluffy!

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:42.660
Wait--is this girl...?

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.040
I haven't introduced myself.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.620
I am Elizabeth, the second
princess of this nation!

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.080
Knew it.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.370
I'm Marie Adler.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:01.580
Why were you in that alley with
no attendants, Your Highness?

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:06.950
We'd come all the way to Gideon
and they wouldn't let me outside.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.910
I sneaked out to do some sightseeing.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:13.830
That explains the guards.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.370
Today I shall let my hair down and enjoy myself!

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.200
So, um...

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.250
What is it?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.910
I'd like you to show me around.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:33.120
Yes, of course. I accept.

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:34.450
Really?

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.250
Sure.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:38.120
Then let's be on our way!

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.040
Where to, Your Highness?

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:45.330
That sounds so distant.

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.950
All right: I'll call you "Ellie."

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:55.000
I like that! I shall be Ellie from now on!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.790
Ellie...

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:40.410
"Chapter 9: The Beginning of Madness"

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.830
"Chapter 9: The Beginning of Madness"

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.830
Assassinating a royal
gets you sent straight to gaol.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:44.080
Assassinating a royal
gets you sent straight to gaol.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.910
Now that your hands have effectively been tied,
there's something I'd like to--

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:52.410
Are you insane?!

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.410
Do you understand what the situation is here?

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:02.540
I kidnapped the second
princess. Now I'm talking.

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:04.790
And just as I try to say something...

00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:06.700
... <i>you</i> come in!

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.080
Why the <i>hell</i> are you attacking?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.620
You don't get it! You <i>don't</i> !

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.000
Maybe you're just an idiot!

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:18.160
Or a hothead, due for a cooling down.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:33.040
That there is an Oxygen Slime.
Working name: Destroyer!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.700
Fire!

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:45.500
Oh, come <i>on</i> . Are you even listening?
That's an <i>Oxygen</i> Slime.

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.620
Do you even know what "oxygen" is?

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:52.830
Morons who put fire near liquid oxygen
will lose their lab privileges!

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:59.370
And besides... Li'l Destroyer here
will just regenerate after it explodes.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:05.370
See, that idiot's got me all off-track.
Let's talk demands!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:07.330
When I press this...

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:13.330
...random monsters pop out of those devices.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:17.830
Although they'll all automatically be released
over the space of an hour anyway,

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:20.160
whether I press it or not.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.790
And there are <i>scads</i> of these things
set up throughout the city.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:28.620
There are two ways to shut them down:

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:34.040
Destroy this switch or get me
to take the death penalty.

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.000
Easy, right?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.040
So, Masters of the kingdom!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:42.290
The game has begun!

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.500
This is ridiculous!

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.910
Why would he announce all this first?

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.660
And why tell us exactly how to win?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:52.700
You're right.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:57.160
This is just a guess, but I think the point
is to make it look preventable

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.910
then have us fail.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:01.500
That must be--

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:04.500
What's going on?

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.290
The lobby. C'mon.

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:09.580
Huh?

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:11.120
Marie?

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.080
Yes! We can do this!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.120
What the--?

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:25.830
Now we've got some lamebrain trying
to brute-force through the barrier.

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:34.080
Hiya! Been a sec, huh?
See, about that barrier...

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:39.410
Every blow releases a monster somewhere in town.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:42.250
If the barrier were to be destroyed,

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:46.120
<i>all</i> of the monsters would be set
free well before the hour is up!

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.290
Damn it all!

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:53.910
This is bad. At this rate, the kingdom's
Masters are bound to fail.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:58.660
Then what? Isn't he just gonna gloat?

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:05.410
Maybe that's all there is to it for us Masters,
but there are tians here, too.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:09.950
The kingdom's poised to lose
before the second war even begins.

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:11.250
Right.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.830
Why attack Gideon?

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:30.370
Just a little entertainment to mark
the end of all that war business.

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:35.870
The mightiest knight and the greatest
mage are dead. So is the king!

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:38.700
The countryfolk are fleeing in despair.

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:43.330
All that and this nation hasn't given up.
Why do you think that is?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:50.330
They lost the last war because their ranked
Masters basically didn't participate.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:52.580
That's the understanding.

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:56.790
And that's pretty much how this
Clash of the Superiors played out.

00:08:56.790 --> 00:09:03.500
Showing off the power of their
Superiors, all "We still got it!"

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.620
Well, it's a <i>big pain</i> .

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:13.120
It'd be a mess if this country's Superiors
all took part in the next war somehow.

00:09:13.120 --> 00:09:18.080
Which is why I'm here now--to break its spirit.

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:20.450
The unreliable Masters of this land,
twiddling their thumbs

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:26.120
as the city is torn to shreds,
their princess is kidnapped...

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:31.040
Why, the tians would have lost
all hope in these Masters--

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:35.040
along with their will to resist.

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.450
You think so?

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:42.370
<i>I</i> find the kingdom's Masters quite dependable.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:50.580
Brother Bear, how strong are the
kingdom's forces outside the arena?

00:09:50.580 --> 00:09:56.040
Masters with battle-oriented jobs
will have come to watch the fights,

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:00.040
so the Masters on the outside
won't be that powerful.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:04.200
But there <i>could</i> be powerful Masters
who just happened not to attend.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.370
Franklin would have taken measures
against any tough guys.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.580
Probably Franklin's people.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:15.370
If that bunch and those monsters
start running amok...

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.250
So we're trapped.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.700
If only this barrier weren't here.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.910
Huh?

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:28.370
You there! Do you have some
kind of barrier-related skill?

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:29.910
N-No...

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:31.870
What's your total level?

00:10:31.870 --> 00:10:33.910
41.

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:36.370
I get it now, grizz!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:41.080
It's an arena barrier!
<i>That's</i> why you can pass through!

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.790
Shu... what on earth--?

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:48.330
This barrier restricts traffic
moving both in and out.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:52.200
But that means nothing to players
at level 50 or below,

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.620
who can't take part in duels
because they pass right through.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:58.620
Oh, right! So that means...

00:10:58.620 --> 00:11:01.910
Request assistance from all
Masters level 50 and below!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:07.160
Masters at level 51 and up with support jobs,
set the rookies up with buffs and autoheals!

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:09.540
You know what this means, right?

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:14.450
Yeah--and I doubt he hasn't
caught onto this loophole.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:19.120
We have a loophole, Ray.
But in all likelihood, it's a trap.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.290
Even if it isn't, we're up against
pro players, an army of monsters...

00:11:22.290 --> 00:11:25.790
...and Franklin, a Superior.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:30.500
You <i>are</i> going to die.
Still ready to forge ahead?

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.790
Let me ask <i>you</i> something, bro:

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:38.330
A girl's been snatched away before my eyes,
and a city's about to be plunged into chaos.

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:44.290
Do you think I could give up?
With <i>this</i> nasty taste in my mouth?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:46.370
I figured you'd say that.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:51.410
I'm out of Brooches, and I'm down
to my last one of these. Take it.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:54.120
I will. Thanks.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:12:02.080
Feel free to go hog wild. Just hang tight
and don't die. I'll be right there.

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:05.500
I know I can count on you... bro.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:11.040
Let's go, Ray.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.160
Yeah!

00:12:15.620 --> 00:12:18.000
Time to fight back!

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:24.250
That Franklin gave us one sweet deal, eh?

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:28.290
Yeah. We just have to take on rookies
who can pass through the barrier

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:33.200
and we'll be sitting pretty
once we defect to Dryfe.

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:37.700
I gotta say, as a former Altar Master,
it does sting a little!

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:43.040
Oh? Because it sure looks like
you're enjoying yourself.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:50.410
Oho. Guess they finally feel like coming out.

00:12:50.410 --> 00:12:51.950
It's quest time.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:54.750
Red, prep an AOE spell.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:57.950
Huh?

00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:01.450
Hellish Miasma! Full blast!

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:05.910
What the...?

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:06.160
"Ryzac" "Intoxication"
"Myanna" "Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness"

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.200
"Ryzac" "Intoxication"
"Myanna" "Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness"

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:09.200
P-Poisonous gas that gives three debuffs?!

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:15.410
How the hell is a rookie
using such powerful gear?

00:13:15.410 --> 00:13:16.160
Red!

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:18.620
Ready and rarin' to go!

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:25.250
Good! Now to rain on our pal's parade!

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:29.620
The hell?

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:35.660
Not again! How does a rookie
wind up with monsters like that?

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.080
Red! Fire off that spell, and fast!

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.700
Crimson Sphe--

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.040
Silence.

00:13:42.830 --> 00:13:44.000
What gives?!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.370
It wasn't me! Someone cancelled my magic!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:57.330
Our forces are still bigger and better.

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.410
Hey! Push 'em back!

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:00.120
On it!

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:02.120
Let's do this!

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.410
What's with the friendly fire?

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:08.830
No way...

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:08.910
"Theodore V Turtle Form"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness"
"Elnath"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness"

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.080
"Theodore V Turtle Form"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness" "Charm"
"Elnath"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness"

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:09.790
"Theodore V Turtle Form"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness" "Charm"
"Elnath"
"Poison" "Intoxication" "Weakness" "Charm"

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.790
"Weakness" "Charm"

00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.790
Charm? But... But that's absurd!

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:15.540
Lilim Temptation!

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.040
"Charm"

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:20.540
Myanna! Hurry up with the recovery!

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.790
What happened? Did they get you?

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:27.290
There's still me and Red...

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:38.410
Crimson Sphere!

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:51.950
Vengeance is Mine!

00:14:54.790 --> 00:14:58.290
If we lose here, our betrayal's all for nothing!

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.040
Think again.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.660
Durandal!

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:24.540
You're finished!

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:51.080
Even a higher-ranked player can be hit
if you just find an opening.

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.290
Right, Liz?

00:15:53.290 --> 00:15:54.450
Dammit.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:59.450
I wouldn't've turned my back on the kingdom
if I'd known they had rookies like <i>that</i> .

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:05.700
That was faster than I'd expected.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.660
What's that you're looking at?

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:09.040
Here.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.410
Are those lights Masters?

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:18.450
Bingo. We're the red,
and the kingdom is the blue.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.660
The kingdom has more than a few on their side,

00:16:21.660 --> 00:16:24.580
powerful folks who didn't come
to today's big event.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.830
Franklin! Help us!

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:29.950
It's the sixth in the duel
rankings, Kamen Rider--

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:33.790
See?

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:36.080
Club. Move to C3.

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:37.000
Club?

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.870
Yep. I prepared these special markers myself.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:53.620
Club, heart, diamond... I don't see any spade.

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:56.410
That won't show up on this map.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.910
Spade's for my plan D, so we
probably won't see them at all.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:01.000
Ah.

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:10.330
Is this map for keeping away from Masters?

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:13.330
I'm a weakling, you see.

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:17.040
Still, the only ones who could get past
the wall of monsters and take me down

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.250
would be my fellow Superiors.

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:43.620
There <i>is</i> someone. A Master without a Superior
Embryo who defeated a Superior.

00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:46.410
The Superior Killer.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:56.250
I should have asked earlier:
Why are we headed west?

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.200
Why?

00:17:58.200 --> 00:18:00.250
It's west.

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:03.120
Something's there.

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:09.040
If the west gate is important somehow...
then he must be blocking it himself.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.540
Marie?

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.410
Yes, Ellie, it's me.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:21.580
I'm glad to see you again. But how--?

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.950
First let's get you someplace safe.
We can talk later.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:28.160
If you want to escape, use this.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:29.370
What is it?

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:30.910
Red means Dryfe.

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:34.290
Oh, I get it. Very useful!

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:43.450
Do you know what these
playing card symbols mean?

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:48.790
The diamond is Franklin.
The heart and club are his confidants.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:57.250
He's taken more than ten times his HP
in fatal damage, but the rat's still alive.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:19:01.700
I've got to get Ellie to the arena. To him.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:04.830
He won't lose--not even against Franklin.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:07.620
We're almost there, Ellie.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:09.290
Okay, Ma--

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:17.000
I'll be taking the princess back now.

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:22.040
I was sure we were far outside
the Castling skill's effective range.

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.620
I Castled via monsters I'd placed in town.

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:30.120
You really did a number on me, Superior Killer.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:34.620
Without monsters to transfer my
damage to, I'd have died for sure.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:38.330
I wanted you to eat that penalty,
at the very least.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:42.580
You're a scary one, all right!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:46.660
Do something with this terror, will you, club?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.580
He'll handle you.

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:59.750
After all, I did bring him here
to deal with exceptions like you.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:14.370
Here I thought you were just
a talented little quartet.

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:20.790
But if you're here, you must be enemies. Right?

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:22.620
Affirmative.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:24.790
May I ask your name?

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:26.450
The club on the board.

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:32.830
Veldorbell, King of Orchestras--
the Superior Conductor job.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:40.540
I see. I'm Marie Adler, Death Shadow--
the Superior Onmitsu job.

00:20:40.540 --> 00:20:43.700
You're in my way, so hurry up and die already.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:49.540
What's the rush, dear listener?
Take in your requiem before you part.

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.750
Is this some kind of joke?

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:56.620
Wait! There's something over there!

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:59.200
One of those Dryfe guys.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:21:01.500
Let's get him!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.830
Cyco. La Porte de l'Enfer.

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:07.290
Understood.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:15.620
Huh? W-Wiped out? But--

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.950
An Embryo skill...

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:21.750
Less than 100, I see. No matter.

00:21:21.750 --> 00:21:23.700
What is <i>this</i> ?

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:27.540
A low number. Probably a support job.

00:21:27.540 --> 00:21:29.660
A Bishop or something.

00:21:29.660 --> 00:21:31.410
Then we have no choice.

00:21:36.540 --> 00:21:38.750
Look, Master.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:46.080
Think you can freeze these
flames, eh? Go on and try!

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.290
You won't pass.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:58.910
My La Porte de l'Enfer ignores temperature.

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:03.410
Gideon's Masters are tough. Much tougher than I.

00:22:03.410 --> 00:22:07.160
Veterans all, with plentiful
experience fighting people.

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:11.660
Which is why... you will never win against me.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.120
Never.

00:23:44.410 --> 00:23:45.750
"The Movement on the Board"

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:47.700
"The Movement on the Board"

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:47.700
"The Movement on the Board."

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:48.370
"The Movement on the Board"
